Package: ciri-support
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Michał Kopeć <michal@nozomi.space>
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Depends: python3, unzip, e2fsprogs, ca-certificates, initramfs-tools
Recommends: iio-sensor-proxy, wireplumber
Homepage: https://github.com/mkopec/ciri-mainline
Description: Configuration and firmware installer for the Lenovo Chromebook Duet (Ciri)
 Configuration for running a mainline kernel on the Lenovo Chromebook Duet
 Gen 9 (Ciri, MediaTek MT8188): the audio UCM profile, the accelerometer
 mount matrix, udev rules for the stylus and the thermal governor, and an
 initramfs hook for the touchscreen firmware.
 .
 The touchscreen and camera firmware is only shipped with ChromeOS and is
 not included. On installation, ciri-firmware-update downloads the official
 ChromeOS recovery image for Ciri from Google and copies the firmware out of
 it. Set CIRI_SUPPORT_SKIP_FIRMWARE=1 to skip this, and run
 ciri-firmware-update later.
